# Keep the working tree byte-identical to what is committed, on every OS.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true rewrites every text
# file to CRLF locally while the repo stores LF. Prettier is configured for LF
# (its default), so `npm run format:check` — which CI runs — then reports every
# file as misformatted on Windows even though it passes on the Linux runner.
# Pinning eol=lf makes the local check agree with CI and silences the
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning on every commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending translated.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.mp4 binary
*.pbf binary
